A||||3||Tom88gt||Transaxle locked in 2nd gear???||||8||
Z||000000||Tom88gt||07-05-2001||06:13 PM||||My Gertrag is suddenly locked in 2nd gear.  It happened after I installed Rodney's Gertrag bronze bushing kit but I don't think that was the cause.  All I know is that the shift lever will only go back into 2nd.  It will not go forward or side-to-side.<P>The Haynes manual says the "lock pin" or "interlock pin" is missing.  But it give no further info and tell you to go to a professional mechanic.  Where is this pin an how does one fix it?<P>Thanks,<BR>Tom||||reg||8
Z||000001||rogergarrison||07-05-2001||06:25 PM||||maybe with the slop out, the linkage cable needs adjusting. try removing the cable from the tranny end and see if you can move the shift levers by hand from there. If you can trans is prob ok. If not its in trans.||||reg||1
Z||000002||mrfiero||07-05-2001||06:27 PM||||Try removing the bushings and replace them with the originals......I agree that this is unlikely to be the culprit, but you need to rule it out.<P>Now, how is the fluid level?  Do your axle seals leak?  It is possible that you "fried" the innards of the tranny (this has happened to me).  <P>Another possibility is the shift rail has broken......this would require major surgery to fix.  I had a shift rail break on me, but I could still shift in th eother gears (lost 2nd & 3rd, but still had 1st, 2nd & 5th).<P>One more possibility (and doubtful too) is your cables have seized.  <P>Let us know about the fluid level and if replacing the new bushings helps.   <p>[This message has been edited by mrfiero (edited 07-05-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||Tom88gt||07-06-2001||12:36 PM||||Oops...I installed one of the shifter brackets wrong.  The one that is a loop, it has a pin on the inside that slips into a groove on the shifter shaft coming out of the transaxle.  I installed it with the pin on top of the shaft and not inside the groove.<P>All is good now.||||reg||11
